            <ArticleTitle>[Primary omental torsion as a cause of acute abdomen: case report].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>554-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5505/tjtes.2011.40222</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Torsion of the omentum is a rare pathology that was described 100 years ago. The characteristic appearance of omental torsion and a review of the literature are presented with respect to a case of primary omental torsion that was causing acute abdomen. Excision of the ischemic omentum is the proper treatment for omental torsion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
